{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphproducts\/tensorproductview"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/Position","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/UndirectedEdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/UndirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/UndirectedIndexRow"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/first","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/second"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView\/Graph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TensorProductView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"First","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Second","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices and their indices are as in ","type":"text"},{"code":"CartesianProductView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The row of (g, h) lists ","type":"text"},{"code":"(g′, h′)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each entry g′ of G’s row of g and each entry h′ of H’s row of h, G outer. Rows are computed from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the factors’ index rows and never hash.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An edge’s position is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position(first: e, second: f, reversed:)"},{"text":": G’s edge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":" and H’s edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"text":". In an undirected product two non-loop edges {a, b} and {c, d} give two edges, the straight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"{(a, c), (b, d)} and the reversed {(a, d), (b, c)}, where a, c are the edges’ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u"},{"text":" ends; when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either is a self-loop they coincide and there is one, not reversed. A row lists a factor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop from its first appearance only, so every product edge has each of its ends once in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rows. Directed, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"text":" is always false, and the product has edge indices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(e)·m_H + index(f)"},{"text":" when both factors have them; undirected it has none, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop changes how many edges a factor pair gives.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tensor product G × H of two graphs, both directed or both undirected, as a lazy view. Made"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tensorProductView(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Also called the direct, categorical or Kronecker product."}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TensorProductView","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:13GraphProducts17TensorProductViewV","title":"TensorProductView","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView.swift#L41","fileName":"TensorProductView.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TensorProductView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProducts"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"references":{"doc://GraphProducts/documentation/GraphProducts":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"GraphProducts","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphproducts"},"doc://GraphProducts/documentation/GraphProducts/TensorProductView/DirectedEdges":{"role":"symbol